    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite is green (21 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied on owner creation, in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **New `normalizeAddress` method**: trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, then expands street-type abbreviations word-by-word using a new `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` map (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A null/blank value normalizes to `\"\"`. Expansion is token-based so it won't mangle words that merely contain an abbreviation (e.g. `STREET` stays `STREET`).\n- **Wired into `addOwner`**: the address is normalized first and written back onto the DTO. This makes the normalized form flow through everything downstream:\n  - The **required-field check** now sees the normalized value, so an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected as a missing `address` \u2192 400.\n  - **Household duplicate detection** compares the normalized address against existing owners' (already-normalized) stored addresses \u2192 409 for equivalent addresses.\n  - The mapper stores and returns the normalized address, and derives **`householdId`** from it, so equivalent addresses share the same household id.\n\nThis satisfies the three new checkpoints (Cp10 household-duplicate, Cp11 shared-household-id, Cp12 address-normalize) and leaves all existing behavior intact.",
